SEC Chairman Atkins: The United States should advance regulatory reform for crypto

1. SEC Chairman Atkins: The United States should advance regulatory reform for crypto; 
​
2. SEC Chairman: Regardless of whether the Clarity Act is passed, the SEC will continue to promote crypto-asset regulation—still to be verified; 
​
3. WTO: The obstacle of stablecoins in international trade is that regulatory frameworks differ; 
​
4. Clemens: Devices were targeted by social engineering attacks, and information was obtained by hackers; 
​
5. Impact Biomedical Inc announced a 1-for-12.62 reverse stock split to move forward with its merger with Zoar Limited; 
​
6. A former California police officer was sentenced to 21 months in prison for misusing law-enforcement credentials; 
​
7. Bitcoin is up 2% today, while the semiconductor index is down 5.9%; 
​
8. A U.S. House committee passed a 114-page crypto tax proposal.
